  "author_association": "NONE",
  "body": "![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cfabcaa5-5a30-4625-be09-853c8d3fee95)\n\nThe difference in memory usage between the LLaMA LLM model and BitNet B1.58 doesn't seem as large as expected, even though they have the same number of parameters. If the LLaMA LLM uses 16-bit precision weights and BitNet uses 1.58-bit weights, the memory usage for LLaMA should be at least 8 times higher. Why is the difference in usage smaller?",
  "closed_at": "2024-10-21T09:07:41Z",
